    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "The full test suite passes (BUILD SUCCESS). Done.\n\nI implemented the `checkDigit` field with these changes:\n\n1. **`CheckDigit.java`** (new helper in `rest/function/owner/`) \u2014 computes the standard Luhn check digit (0-9) over the digits of a customer code, ignoring the hyphens; returns `null` when the code is absent.\n\n2. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added a read-only `checkDigit` integer property (0-9) to the Owner schema, so the generated `OwnerDto` gains the field.\n\n3. **`OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 wired a MapStruct `@Mapping` expression that populates `checkDigit` from `CheckDigit.of(owner.getCustomerCode())`.\n\nThe algorithm mirrors the test's own `luhn(...)` reference implementation exactly, so `GET /api/owners/{id}` now returns a `checkDigit` equal to the Luhn digit of the returned `customerCode`. `AcceptanceTest` and the full suite are green.",
